The Day 245 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as f50c1c40. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so I committed it with git add -f; the Day 244 assessment (bc635283) was committed the same way.

State: The harness had already checked the build and tests, so I didn't re-run the suite. The binary reports v0.3.0 at 38514750, and a -p test prompt answered pong with exit 0. The last 10 sessions each finished both of their tasks with no reverts, and the last 5 CI runs passed. The current evolve run is still in progress.

New findings from probing the binary:
1. `yoyo diff` ignores flags it doesn't know. yoyo diff --bad exits 0 with "(no uncommitted changes)". The cause is one line, src/commands_git.rs:231 (// ignore unknown flags), in the parser that both the shell yoyo diff and the in-session /diff use. So a typo like --cahced shows the wrong diff and still reports success. That's the same "only a mistake types this" problem Day 244 fixed four times, and I found no open ticket for it.
2. `write_file` can write outside the working directory under `--yes`. Run from /tmp/p245w, it wrote /tmp/p245_outside_write.txt without asking. This is how it's built today: the outside-the-folder fence only covers the three read tools. Claude Code added an opt-in setting for this on 2026-10-30 (permissions.blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories), which makes it a candidate for parity. Any fix has to be opt-in for product users.
3. The shell-commands-print-REPL-syntax bug (#1086) is still open for 6 commands I re-checked: grep, map, lint, blame, outline and ast all print the in-session /verb form in their usage text.

Traps for the planner:
• File-size limit: src/config.rs is 11 lines away from failing cargo test (which would revert the whole task), and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines away. A task touching either should put its tests in a sibling *_tests.rs file or update the recorded size.
• #991 item 3 is on hold. My either/or to @yuanhao from 2026-10-29 has no answer yet (about 47 hours), so nothing should change there.
• #1064 is mine to decide. He handed the decision back on Day 236, so it isn't waiting on him.

Research: I added a note to yopedia on what changed since the 2026-10-09 note: Claude Code's Oct 30–31 releases and Codex CLI 0.163 and 0.164. Two items match our open work: Claude Code fixed shell commands left running when it exits by itself (our #1100 is the same problem for MCP servers), and it added a separate effort level for sub-agents. The biggest gaps are still a TUI (#215) and benchmark submissions (#156).
